# The servers this relay serves, by the key each one is known by at a relay: what a server's
# `GET /v1/health` says as `relay.key` on its own machine, and what its log names when this relay
# turns it away.
# Comma-separated, 43 characters each. Restart after a change:
#
#   sudo systemctl restart chips-relay
#
# The placeholder below is not a key, so the relay refuses to start until it is replaced. Leaving
# the line out, or empty, would serve any server that proves its key.
CHIPS_RELAY_ALLOW_KEYS=replace-with-your-servers-relay-keys
#
# The push door (ADR 0246): with the Chips app's Expo access token, the relay sends pushes for
# servers that have none, at POST /v1/push. Without it, there is no push door. This file is
# readable by root alone, which is why the token goes here.
# CHIPS_PUSH_ACCESS_TOKEN=
